1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,966
Explore our New Homes on the map.

2
00:00:02,966 --> 00:00:11,450
Search by area or postcode, filter by bedrooms and budget, and
add stations, transport lines and landmarks.

3
00:00:12,350 --> 00:00:21,698
Open a development to explore its photography, videos,
description, features and amenities.

4
00:00:21,698 --> 00:00:27,450
Check the bedroom options and confirmed starting prices.

5
00:00:28,350 --> 00:00:33,964
See the nearest stations and check how long it takes to walk or
cycle to them.

6
00:00:33,964 --> 00:00:38,211
In the commute section, enter a destination and choose your

7
00:00:38,211 --> 00:00:41,450
travel mode to open the route in Google Maps.

8
00:00:42,350 --> 00:00:46,300
Buyers can save favourites without signing in, share a
development with someone

9
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:49,450
else, or send their shortlist back to their broker on WhatsApp.

10
00:00:50,350 --> 00:00:54,291
Add your photo, job title and WhatsApp number in My Profile.

11
00:00:54,291 --> 00:00:58,560
Your personal portfolio link keeps you as the contact buyers
see.

12
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:01,450
Use it instead of the generic homepage link.

13
00:01:02,350 --> 00:01:08,378
Create saved collections for different requirements, such as
Prime Central London.

14
00:01:08,378 --> 00:01:13,450
Choose the developments and share a map with those homes
highlighted.

15
00:01:14,350 --> 00:01:19,127
Choose which lines and stations appear when your collection
opens.

16
00:01:19,127 --> 00:01:23,397
If your buyer wants to live near the Elizabeth line, select

17
00:01:23,397 --> 00:01:27,450
it and show its stations, then save and share that view.

18
00:01:28,350 --> 00:01:31,987
Use a saved collection to create a branded brochure.

19
00:01:31,987 --> 00:01:40,450
Choose the default London cover or a development image,
introduce the selection, and include your broker contact
details.

20
00:01:41,350 --> 00:01:47,048
Add a personalised note for each development explaining why you
have included it.

21
00:01:47,048 --> 00:01:53,450
The notes appear on the development pages of your brochure,
alongside the property details.

22
00:01:54,350 --> 00:01:58,673
Save the brochure in your workspace to reopen and adapt for
future buyers.

23
00:01:58,673 --> 00:02:01,769
Regenerate the PDF with the latest portfolio details.

24
00:02:01,769 --> 00:02:05,450
Download it, or prepare an Outlook email with the PDF attached.

25
00:02:06,350 --> 00:02:11,527
Our JLL stock imports listing copy and imagery from the
Residential New Homes website.

26
00:02:11,527 --> 00:02:14,116
The website is our default source of truth.

27
00:02:14,116 --> 00:02:18,450
Manual edits are protected, with website differences flagged for
review.

28
00:02:19,350 --> 00:02:24,295
Paste a developer's listing URL to extract as much available
information as possible.

29
00:02:24,295 --> 00:02:29,298
Review the imagery and copy, complete missing details, then
confirm before publishing.

30
00:02:29,298 --> 00:02:31,450
Some websites need manual completion.

31
00:02:32,350 --> 00:02:34,344
Hundreds of developments to add?

32
00:02:34,344 --> 00:02:38,082
Use bulk JSON upload to bring in up to 200 records per file.

33
00:02:38,082 --> 00:02:40,450
Review every record before publishing.

34
00:02:41,350 --> 00:02:45,765
Google Analytics shows visits, development views, favourites and
WhatsApp clicks.

35
00:02:45,765 --> 00:02:50,016
Team activity shows sign-ins, last use, saved collections and
sharing actions.

36
00:02:50,016 --> 00:02:53,450
Filter the team report, compare periods and export the results.

37
00:02:54,350 --> 00:02:55,702
Complete your profile.

38
00:02:55,702 --> 00:02:57,115
Build your collections.

39
00:02:57,115 --> 00:02:59,450
Share a portfolio that feels personal.
